From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:26:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: create, add to and leave group DMs from the Messaging
 app

* Create group DMs from the Messaging app

The Messaging app can now start a group. The transport emits
"webos-im-group-create" with the account, a name and the members'
buddy names joined by "\x1f".

A Discord group outside a server is a group DM. The handler resolves
each member to a user id, as send_im does when it opens a DM, and
POSTs the ids as "recipients" to /users/@me/channels. When that
answers with a group DM and a name was given, it PATCHes the channel's
name. Nothing else is needed for the app to see the group: the gateway
sends CHANNEL_CREATE, which discord_got_group_dm already turns into a
buddy list chat.

It returns TRUE once the request is on its way. For an account that is
not Discord's, no members, or a member the plug-in does not know it
returns FALSE and creates nothing, rather than a group without someone
the user picked.

The member list splitting and the request body are in webos_helpers.c,
with unit tests.

* Add people to a group DM from the Messaging app

The Messaging app can now add members to a group. The transport emits
"webos-im-group-invite" with the account, the group's chat (its channel
id) and the new members' buddy names joined by "\x1f".

Only a group DM has members of its own to add. For one, the handler
resolves each name to a user and PUTs it to
/channels/{id}/recipients/{user}, the request discord_chat_invite makes
and which now lives in a function both use. A member the plug-in does
not know is skipped and logged. It returns TRUE when at least one
request went out, and FALSE for an account that is not Discord's, a
1:1 DM (Discord cannot turn one into a group) or a server channel:
there, discord_chat_invite POSTs an invite link, which adds nobody.

* Leave group DMs from the Messaging app and with /leave

The Messaging app can now leave a group. The transport emits
"webos-im-group-leave" with the account and the group's chat.

For a group DM the handler sends DELETE /channels/{id}, which leaves
it, and takes the group off the buddy list once Discord answers with
the channel: the plug-in does not handle the gateway's CHANNEL_DELETE.
For anything else it returns FALSE and does nothing. In a 1:1 DM the
request would only close the DM, and a server channel cannot be left
on its own; leaving the whole server is not what leaving a group
means.

/leave in a group DM now leaves it too; it used to do nothing. The
commented-out body of discord_chat_leave_by_room_id stays as it is:
libpurple calls chat_leave whenever a conversation is closed, which
must not take the user out of the group.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
